<title>USA: N.Y. business loans rose $66 mln in March 26 wk.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans rose $66 mln in March 26 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $66 million to $45,339 billion in the week ended March 26, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $68 million to $45,601 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $6,719 million to $834,453 billion.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
</text>
